{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/pulls/459","id":4796488424,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQbBgUs8AAAABHeSa6A","html_url":"https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/459","diff_url":"https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/459.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/459.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/issues/459","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/pulls/459/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/pulls/459/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/issues/459/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MChartier/calibrate-health/statuses/18cf84a2a4d5acc05ca14ecd2ddd861a1fe20b43","number":459,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Remove runtime backend selection and safely bind native sessions to build targets","user":{"login":"MChartier","id":1258197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTgxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1258197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier","html_url":"https://github.com/MChartier","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MChartier/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nCalibrate users should not need to choose a backend. Native sign-in and Advanced settings currently expose that choice. Native tokens are stored separately from the selected origin, so removing the choice also requires a safe startup transition.\n\nThis removes runtime selectors, URL route inputs and self-hosting promotion. Native/internal builds use the validated existing build input; production browsers use their serving origin. Native startup retains matching sessions, requires fresh sign-in for a safely changed target, and blocks unknown or unfinished local state without deleting it. Existing queues also prevent late authentication, logout and storage work from overwriting a replacement session.\n\nFixes #438. Focused successor to #450; #439 and #402 remain historical, with backend administrator/bootstrap work deferred and preserved. No unmerged parent dependency. [Complete scope and retained originals](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/1f48682f47db90555f704637059fa2db0b8f4812/managed-438/focused-followup/scope.json).\n\n## Test plan and behavior evidence\n\n| Scenario | Expected and observed |\n| --- | --- |\n| Open settings and auth/recovery routes, including a misleading server URL parameter | Diagnostics and updates remain; no service editor or promotion. Browser recovery posts to the serving origin, including a retryable synthetic failure. Four maintained Chromium tests and matched captures pass. |\n| Start native storage with matching, changed, missing or malformed legacy identity; interrupt reads/writes; retain queued changes or drafts | Matching credentials survive. A safe changed target starts signed out; pending/failed/replaying, unreadable or unknown state blocks and preserves originals. Maintained storage/state/provider tests pass. |\n| Finish old login/register/refresh or logout after replacement | Replacement credentials, workspace and browser cookie remain owned by the replacement. The unchanged-master native harness reproduces three failures; focused regressions pass. Real browser Set-Cookie tests cover both response-order intentions using the production logout queue. |\n\n[Exact test results, source/build identities and reproduction steps](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/19031ef5d6e23cdb66b24c839889082b9861a6ed/managed-438/focused-final/provenance.json). Synthetic fixtures only; no live account migration.\n\n### Before / After\n\nAdvanced settings removes hosting promotion while retaining support diagnostics and software updates.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: Advanced settings with self-hosting guidance](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/19031ef5d6e23cdb66b24c839889082b9861a6ed/managed-438/focused-final/before-advanced.png) | ![After: Advanced settings with diagnostics and updates](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/19031ef5d6e23cdb66b24c839889082b9861a6ed/managed-438/focused-final/after-advanced.png) |\n\nRecovery remains on the serving origin despite an incoming server URL parameter. The same synthetic failure still offers retry guidance.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: recovery failure on serving origin](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/19031ef5d6e23cdb66b24c839889082b9861a6ed/managed-438/focused-final/before-recovery-failure.png) | ![After: recovery failure on serving origin](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/19031ef5d6e23cdb66b24c839889082b9861a6ed/managed-438/focused-final/after-recovery-failure.png) |\n\nBefore: actual master `547206a1b372b73fc95fc412ad453b8099440000`. After: `8466b29695e6924db0ecbde0a435b04c49f56fc0`; later changes only tighten native consent validation and make native-storage declarations private. [Applicability to current head](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/1f48682f47db90555f704637059fa2db0b8f4812/managed-438/focused-followup/applicability.json) is recorded without relabeling these captures. Independent clean-cache exports, Chromium 149, 1280×1100, scale 1, light theme, fixed clock and identical fixtures. Shared fixture normalization hides unrelated transient PWA notices. [All four pairs and exact image/harness/provenance identities](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/19031ef5d6e23cdb66b24c839889082b9861a6ed/managed-438/focused-final/manifest.json); an initial stale-cache attempt is explicitly retained and excluded.\n\n## Supporting checks and limitations\n\nFull client suite: 234 suites / 1,347 tests passed; final affected suites, TypeScript, app-config and browser checks passed. All 25 current-head CI checks are terminal: 14 passed, 11 skipped, none failed, including Android/iOS builds, web smoke/export, runtime bundles, typechecks and security scanning. The [review bot refused solely due to its quota](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/459#issuecomment-6075059975); no completed current-head bot review is claimed or retried. Independent engineering review/QA remains required.\n\nNative-device execution remains deferred/unexecuted; browser and component results do not claim device validation. Independent QA is pending. Actual GitHub-page rendering was not checked under the human waiver; genuine image pixels were inspected. Predecessor branches, original evidence and deferred backend scope remain preserved on accessible nonmerged refs.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-09T05:41:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:02:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"7eab3f95015906acb29828f87d2c60770362ac92","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"MChartier:fix/managed-first-438-focused","ref":"fix/managed-first-438-focused","repo":{"id":1102078034,"node_id":"R_kgDOQbBgUg","name":"calibrate-health","full_name":"MChartier/calibrate-health","owner":{"login":"MChartier"